description: seo-audit — project overview and architecture
alwaysApply: true
---

`seo-audit` is a Go CLI that crawls a site, runs SEO/technical checks,
scores it 0-100, and acts as a CI quality gate for a separate Go CI runner
project. It runs standalone (human use, text output) and inside CI
(machine use, JSON output + exit codes).

Stack: Go, Cobra (`spf13/cobra`), `golang.org/x/net/html` or GoQuery,
standard `net/http`, `fatih/color` for terminal output, plain Go `testing`.

Package layout:
```
cmd/            — Cobra commands
internal/crawler/    — HTTP fetch, URL frontier, robots.txt, rate limiting
internal/parser/     — HTML -> PageData
internal/checks/     — Check implementations (see Check interface)
internal/scoring/    — PageData + check results -> 0-100 score
internal/report/     — Text + JSON report generation
internal/regression/ — Baseline comparison
```

Data flows one direction: Crawler -> Parser -> Checks -> Scoring -> Report
-> Regression. Don't skip layers or let a later stage reach back into an
earlier one's internals.
